{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:ModelsOfQous.SelfDualCurvature","@type":"LeanModule","name":"ModelsOfQous.SelfDualCurvature","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic","lean:module:QOU.Glossary","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CRRealisation","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Category","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Functor.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.NatTrans","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.ContinuousMap.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Geometry.Manifold.IsManifold.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.InnerProductSpace.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.ExteriorAlgebra.Basic"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.self_dual_curvature","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.self_dual_curvature","kind":"theorem","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/self-dual-curvature.lean#L39-L52","doc":"**Proposition (Self-duality of the curvature).**\nWhen `dim_ℝ M = 5` (CR dimension `n = 2`, so `dim_ℝ H = 4`), the\ncurvature of an instanton connection, restricted to `H`, is self-dual\nwith respect to the Hodge star `*_H` determined by the Webster metric.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{prop:self-dual-curvature}`\nProof: The contact form `θ` splits `TM = H ⊕ ℝξ`.  By the Bogomolny\ndecomposition, `YM(A) = ∫‖F⁺‖² + ∫‖F⁻‖²`.  Minimisation forces\n`F⁻ = 0`, which is precisely `⋆_H F_A|_H = F_A|_H`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:ex:self-dual-curvature","label":"ex:self-dual-curvature","md":"quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/self-dual-curvature.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}